      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to expand the product \\((3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x)\\) and express the result in the form \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d\\). We will then find the values of \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\) and use these to compute \\(8a + 4b + 2c + d\\).\n\nFirst, let's expand the product:\n\n\\[\n(3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x)\n\\]\n\nWe will use the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials, but extended to trinomials) to expand this product.\n\n1. Distribute \\(3x^2\\) to each term in the second polynomial:\n   \\[\n   3x^2 \\cdot 7 + 3x^2 \\cdot (-2x) = 21x^2 - 6x^3\n   \\]\n\n2. Distribute \\(-5x\\) to each term in the second polynomial:\n   \\[\n   -5x \\cdot 7 + (-5x) \\cdot (-2x) = -35x + 10x^2\n   \\]\n\n3. Distribute \\(4\\) to each term in the second polynomial:\n   \\[\n   4 \\cdot 7 + 4 \\cdot (-2x) = 28 - 8x\n   \\]\n\nNow, combine all these results:\n\\[\n21x^2 - 6x^3 - 35x + 10x^2 + 28 - 8x\n\\]\n\nNext, combine like terms:\n\\[\n-6x^3 + (21x^2 + 10x^2) + (-35x - 8x) + 28\n\\]\n\nSimplify:\n\\[\n-6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28\n\\]\n\nThis is now in the form \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d\\), where:\n\\[\na = -6, \\quad b = 31, \\quad c = -43, \\quad d = 28\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to calculate \\(8a + 4b + 2c + d\\):\n\n\\[\n8a + 4b + 2c + d = 8(-6) + 4(31) + 2(-43) + 28\n\\]\n\nFirst, compute each term:\n\\[\n8(-6) = -48\n\\]\n\\[\n4(31) = 124\n\\]\n\\[\n2(-43) = -86\n\\]\n\\[\n28 = 28\n\\]\n\nNow, sum these values:\n\\[\n-48 + 124 - 86 + 28\n\\]\n\nPerform the addition and subtraction step-by-step:\n\\[\n-48 + 124 = 76\n\\]\n\\[\n76 - 86 = -10\n\\]\n\\[\n-10 + 28 = 18\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{18}\n\\]",
